{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Recipe",
  "recipeCuisine": "France",
  "name": "Herb Crêpes",
  "text": "Herb Crêpes\n\nPreparation time:\n\nCooking time:\n\nIngredients\n\n60g plain flour,\n\n150ml milk,\n\n2 eggs,\n\n15g mixed herbs (parsley, chervil, chives; chopped),\n\n30g clarified butter.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Put the flour in a bowl, season, and make a well in the centre.\n\n2. Add one-third of the milk and the eggs then whisk lightly to make a smooth batter.\n\n3. Pour in the rest of the milk and mix thoroughly.\n\n4. Pass the batter through a chinois or fine sieve.\n\n5. Add the chopped herbs.\n\n5. Cover with cling film and leave to rest for at least 30 minutes in the fridge.",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "60g plain flour,",
    "150ml milk,",
    "2 eggs,",
    "15g mixed herbs (parsley, chervil, chives; chopped),",
    "30g clarified butter."
  ],
  "recipeInstructions": [
